    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495-a1">

                <pb facs="1321" n="1315" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1315"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">The <hi rendition="#small-caps">President</hi>:</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State has the honor to lay before the President a copy of a
                    dispatch, with its accompaniment, from our minister at Honolulu, No. 51, of
                    April 14, 1894.</p>
                <p>Mr. Willis’s dispatches, numbered 49 and 50, are dated April 13, 1894. The former
                    acknowledges instructions numbered 17 to 21, inclusive, and the latter transmits
                    a receipt for the Department’s cipher volume and holocryptic code.</p>
                <p>Respectfully submitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
